# Subscriptions

Package tiers are the hard upper bound on access. See `permissions.mdc` for the effective-access formula.

## Tiers

- `Free`: `app_shell`, `auth_session`, `general_settings`, `patient_registry`. Reporting (`reports_audit` / `reporting-analytics`) is platform infrastructure on every package.
- `Basic`: Free plus tenant, facility, access admin, OPD, triage, clinical, limited IPD, pharmacy dispense, billing. Emergency, rooms/beds, and communications are version-disabled.
- `Advanced`: Basic plus full IPD, nursing, discharge, lab, radiology, pharmacy clinical, and claims. Physiotherapy is version-disabled.
- `Pro`: Advanced plus ICU, theater, HR, and dental when enabled. Biomedical, operations, housekeeping, mortuary, and integrations are version-disabled.
- `Custom`: Tenant-specific subset or extension of Pro; every entitlement must be explicit and still respect version-disabled domains.
- `Developer`: Non-production only; may include `demo_seed` manage.

## Enforcement

- Package checks must run in UI and API paths.
- Grants must not exceed the active package.
- Version-disabled domains must stay omitted from plan caps and effective access.
- Package changes, resets, upgrades, and downgrades must be atomic and auditable.
- Failed changes must roll back completely.

